# Copy to .env and uncomment what you need. Everything here is optional —
# the tool works with none of these set, and everything here also has a
# widget in the app's own Settings dialog (tray icon or chip → right-click →
# Settings…) if you'd rather not edit a file at all. Full descriptions:
# README.md#configuration.

# --- Display ---
# USAGE_HUD_MODE=chip
# USAGE_HUD_MODE=quiet
# USAGE_HUD_QUIET=1
# USAGE_HUD_OPACITY=0.94
# USAGE_HUD_REFRESH_SECONDS=180
# USAGE_HUD_POPUP_SECONDS=12
# USAGE_HUD_PRESENTATION=1

# --- Alerts ---
# USAGE_HUD_ALERT_INCLUDED_PCT=85
# USAGE_HUD_ALERT_ONDEMAND_PCT=70
# USAGE_HUD_ALERT_BURN_MULTIPLIER=2.0

# --- Providers: hide what you don't pay for (also tray → Providers) ---
# USAGE_HUD_DISABLE=openai,anthropic,opencode-go,cloud
# USAGE_HUD_ENABLE_CLOUD=1

# --- Paths & advanced overrides (auto-detected by default) ---
# USAGE_HUD_STATE_DIR=C:\Users\you\AppData\Roaming\usage-hud
# CURSOR_STATE_DB=C:\Users\you\AppData\Roaming\Cursor\User\globalStorage\state.vscdb
# CURSOR_SESSION_TOKEN=sub::jwt
# OPENCODE_AUTH_JSON=C:\Users\you\.local\share\opencode\auth.json
# OPENCODE_ANTIGRAVITY_JSON=C:\Users\you\.config\opencode\antigravity-accounts.json
# GITHUB_COPILOT_TOKEN=...

# Claude reads local files only — no token, no network call:
# CLAUDE_DESKTOP_DIR=C:\Users\you\AppData\Roaming\Claude
# CLAUDE_JSON=C:\Users\you\.claude.json

# GitHub Actions/storage billing — not an AI service, and off by default;
# setting a token here (or in Settings → Services → GitHub) is what turns it on:
# GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_...
# GITHUB_LOGIN=your-github-login
